---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
const title = 'The teaching layer';
const subtitle = 'Same diff. With and without the explanation wrapped around it.';
---
<Base title={title} description={subtitle}>
  <article class="etude-page">
    <header class="etude-head">
      <p class="etude-kicker">Etude · The anti-cascader</p>
      <h1 class="etude-title">{title}</h1>
      <p class="etude-relief">{subtitle}</p>
      <nav class="etude-nav">
        <a href="/etudes/anti-cascader/">← anti-cascader etudes</a>
        <span class="etude-nav-sep">·</span>
        <a href="/puzzles/bob-the-fixer-as-anti-cascader/">essay</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <section class="etude-intro">
      <p>The codemod produces a diff. <strong>Always the same diff.</strong> What changes is the layer wrapped around it — what the team sees before they read the patch, what they read alongside it, what they take into review.</p>
      <p>Toggle the layer. Then answer four questions about the same migration step.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="etude-stage">
      <div class="etude-card">
        <p class="etude-step">Migration step · javax → jakarta</p>

        <div class="layer-toggle" role="tablist" aria-label="View">
          <button type="button" class="layer-btn layer-btn-active" data-mode="bare" role="tab" aria-selected="true">
            <span class="layer-dot"></span>
            <span class="layer-name">Bare codemod</span>
            <span class="layer-meta">"do the work"</span>
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="layer-btn" data-mode="taught" role="tab" aria-selected="false">
            <span class="layer-dot"></span>
            <span class="layer-name">With teaching layer</span>
            <span class="layer-meta">"teach while doing"</span>
          </button>
        </div>

        <div id="layer-stage" class="layer-stage" aria-live="polite"></div>
      </div>

      <div class="etude-card layer-quiz" id="quiz-card">
        <p class="etude-step">Reader check · 4 questions</p>
        <p class="quiz-help">After you read the surface above (either mode), answer from what's on screen. No outside knowledge.</p>
        <ol class="quiz-list" id="quiz-list"></ol>
        <div id="quiz-result" class="quiz-result" aria-live="polite"></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="etude-failure">
      <h2 class="etude-failure-title">The load-bearing inversion</h2>
      <p>The bare codemod ships the artifact. The taught codemod ships <em>the artifact + the model the team needs to review it</em>. Same lines of code. Different review experience. Different next-time velocity.</p>
      <p>Every surveyed AI coding tool's stance is "do the work" — Cursor, Continue, Aider, Cody, Copilot, Sweep. <strong>None ship the active teaching layer.</strong> The codemod-engine layer is mature; the team-side teacher is the gap.</p>
    </section>

    <footer class="etude-coda">
      <p>The codemod is the deliverable. The explanation is the work.</p>
    </footer>
  </article>
</Base>

<script is:inline>
  // Same diff, two surfaces. The toggle re-renders the stage; the quiz lives
  // below it so the reader can flip between modes and answer from whichever
  // surface gives them a working model. Bare wins on speed; taught wins on
  // questions 2-4 — the ones a reviewer actually has to answer.

  const DIFF_FILES = [
    {
      name: 'src/main/java/com/example/orders/Order.java',
      hunks: [
        { kind: 'del', text: 'import javax.persistence.Entity;' },
        { kind: 'del', text: 'import javax.persistence.Id;' },
        { kind: 'add', text: 'import jakarta.persistence.Entity;' },
        { kind: 'add', text: 'import jakarta.persistence.Id;' },
        { kind: 'ctx', text: '' },
        { kind: 'ctx', text: '@Entity' },
        { kind: 'ctx', text: 'public class Order {' },
        { kind: 'ctx', text: '    @Id private Long id;' },
      ]
    },
    {
      name: 'src/main/java/com/example/orders/web/OrderFilter.java',
      hunks: [
        { kind: 'del', text: 'import javax.servlet.Filter;' },
        { kind: 'del', text: 'import javax.servlet.FilterChain;' },
        { kind: 'add', text: 'import jakarta.servlet.Filter;' },
        { kind: 'add', text: 'import jakarta.servlet.FilterChain;' },
        { kind: 'ctx', text: '' },
        { kind: 'ctx', text: 'public class OrderFilter implements Filter {' },
      ]
    },
    {
      name: 'src/main/java/com/example/orders/api/CreateOrderDto.java',
      hunks: [
        { kind: 'del', text: 'import javax.validation.constraints.NotBlank;' },
        { kind: 'add', text: 'import jakarta.validation.constraints.NotBlank;' },
        { kind: 'ctx', text: '' },
        { kind: 'ctx', text: 'public record CreateOrderDto(@NotBlank String sku) {}' },
      ]
    }
  ];

  const TEACH = {
    title: 'Step 02 of 7 — rename javax.* → jakarta.*',
    why: 'Spring Boot 3 moved the platform-level packages from the <code>javax</code> namespace to <code>jakarta</code>. This is a Jakarta EE change that Spring inherits — every entity, servlet, validation, annotation, and JMS import shifts namespace.',
    transform: 'Mechanical, byte-deterministic. The codemod walks the AST and rewrites import declarations + fully-qualified references in a known set of namespaces.',
    in_scope: [
      'javax.persistence.* → jakarta.persistence.*',
      'javax.servlet.* → jakarta.servlet.*',
      'javax.validation.* → jakarta.validation.*',
      'javax.annotation.* → jakarta.annotation.*',
    ],
    out_of_scope: [
      'javax.crypto.*, javax.naming.*, javax.sql.* — these stayed on javax.',
      'reflection-based class names (e.g. <code>Class.forName("javax.persistence.Entity")</code>) — needs a separate audit.',
      'XML config (<code>web.xml</code>, <code>persistence.xml</code>) — handled in step 04.',
    ],
    review_focus: 'Skim a few files; confirm no <code>javax.crypto</code>/<code>naming</code>/<code>sql</code> imports were touched. Run your tests. The diff is large but the failure mode is narrow: a wrongly-rewritten import fails at compile.',
    next: 'Step 03 rewrites <code>application.{yml,properties}</code> keys. After this PR merges, invoke <code>/migrate-spring-boot-3</code> again.'
  };

  const QUESTIONS = [
    {
      q: 'Which namespaces does this step rewrite?',
      a: ['Every javax.* package', 'Only persistence + servlet + validation + annotation', 'Whichever ones your repo imports'],
      correct: 1,
      seenIn: 'taught',
      why: 'The taught surface lists the four in-scope namespaces explicitly. The bare diff only shows the namespaces that happen to appear in this repo — you can\'t tell from the diff whether <code>javax.crypto</code> would also be rewritten.'
    },
    {
      q: 'If your code uses <code>javax.crypto.Cipher</code>, does this step touch it?',
      a: ['Yes — all javax becomes jakarta', 'No — javax.crypto stayed on javax', 'Can\'t tell from this diff'],
      correct: 1,
      seenIn: 'taught',
      why: 'The taught surface explicitly calls out javax.crypto / naming / sql as out of scope. The bare diff is silent — a reviewer with a crypto-heavy module has to guess.'
    },
    {
      q: 'A class is loaded by name with <code>Class.forName("javax.persistence.Entity")</code>. Will this PR break it?',
      a: ['No — codemod handles strings too', 'Yes — reflection class names are out of scope here', 'Probably, run tests and find out'],
      correct: 1,
      seenIn: 'taught',
      why: 'The taught surface flags reflection-based class names as out of scope. The bare diff has no way to surface this — the reviewer doesn\'t know what was deliberately left.'
    },
    {
      q: 'What should a reviewer focus on when reading this PR?',
      a: ['Read every line carefully', 'Skim a few files; confirm the right namespaces; run tests', 'Block until the platform team responds'],
      correct: 1,
      seenIn: 'taught',
      why: 'The taught surface tells the reviewer exactly what review shape fits this diff. The bare PR description ("automated migration to Spring Boot 3") gives a label but no review protocol.'
    }
  ];

  const stage = document.getElementById('layer-stage');
  const buttons = document.querySelectorAll('.layer-btn');
  const quizList = document.getElementById('quiz-list');
  const quizResult = document.getElementById('quiz-result');

  function renderDiff() {
    const filesHtml = DIFF_FILES.map(f => {
      const lines = f.hunks.map(h => {
        const cls = h.kind === 'add' ? 'd-add' : h.kind === 'del' ? 'd-del' : 'd-ctx';
        const sigil = h.kind === 'add' ? '+' : h.kind === 'del' ? '-' : ' ';
        return `<div class="d-line ${cls}"><span class="d-sigil">${sigil}</span><span class="d-text">${escapeHtml(h.text)}</span></div>`;
      }).join('');
      return `
        <div class="d-file">
          <div class="d-file-name">${escapeHtml(f.name)}</div>
          <div class="d-hunk">${lines}</div>
        </div>`;
    }).join('');
    return `
      <div class="bare-pr">
        <div class="bare-pr-head">
          <span class="bare-pr-state">Open</span>
          <span class="bare-pr-title">automated migration to Spring Boot 3</span>
        </div>
        <p class="bare-pr-meta"><strong>@agent-codemod-7</strong> · 2 files · +10 −10</p>
        <p class="bare-pr-desc">automated migration step from RFC-094</p>
        ${filesHtml}
      </div>
    `;
  }

  function renderTeach() {
    const inScope = TEACH.in_scope.map(s => `<li>${s}</li>`).join('');
    const outScope = TEACH.out_of_scope.map(s => `<li>${s}</li>`).join('');
    return `
      <div class="teach-wrap">
        <div class="teach-explain">
          <p class="teach-card-title">${TEACH.title}</p>
          <p class="teach-row"><span class="teach-label">Why</span><span class="teach-body">${TEACH.why}</span></p>
          <p class="teach-row"><span class="teach-label">How</span><span class="teach-body">${TEACH.transform}</span></p>
          <div class="teach-row teach-row-stack">
            <span class="teach-label">In scope</span>
            <ul class="teach-list">${inScope}</ul>
          </div>
          <div class="teach-row teach-row-stack">
            <span class="teach-label">Out of scope</span>
            <ul class="teach-list">${outScope}</ul>
          </div>
          <p class="teach-row"><span class="teach-label">Review focus</span><span class="teach-body">${TEACH.review_focus}</span></p>
          <p class="teach-row"><span class="teach-label">Next</span><span class="teach-body">${TEACH.next}</span></p>
        </div>
        <div class="teach-diff">
          <p class="teach-diff-label">Diff (same as bare mode)</p>
          ${renderDiff()}
        </div>
      </div>
    `;
  }

  function escapeHtml(s) {
    return String(s).replace(/[&<>]/g, c => ({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;'}[c]));
  }

  function setMode(mode) {
    buttons.forEach(b => {
      const on = b.dataset.mode === mode;
      b.classList.toggle('layer-btn-active', on);
      b.setAttribute('aria-selected', on ? 'true' : 'false');
    });
    stage.innerHTML = mode === 'bare' ? renderDiff() : renderTeach();
    stage.dataset.mode = mode;
  }

  buttons.forEach(b => b.addEventListener('click', () => setMode(b.dataset.mode)));
  setMode('bare');

  // === quiz ===
  const answers = new Array(QUESTIONS.length).fill(null);

  function renderQuiz() {
    quizList.innerHTML = QUESTIONS.map((q, qi) => `
      <li class="quiz-item">
        <p class="quiz-q">${q.q}</p>
        <div class="quiz-opts">
          ${q.a.map((opt, oi) => `
            <button type="button" class="quiz-opt" data-q="${qi}" data-o="${oi}">${opt}</button>
          `).join('')}
        </div>
        <div class="quiz-feedback" id="qf-${qi}"></div>
      </li>
    `).join('');
    quizList.querySelectorAll('.quiz-opt').forEach(btn => {
      btn.addEventListener('click', () => answer(parseInt(btn.dataset.q, 10), parseInt(btn.dataset.o, 10)));
    });
  }

  function answer(qi, oi) {
    if (answers[qi] !== null) return;
    answers[qi] = oi;
    const q = QUESTIONS[qi];
    const correct = oi === q.correct;
    const fbEl = document.getElementById(`qf-${qi}`);
    quizList.querySelectorAll(`.quiz-opt[data-q="${qi}"]`).forEach(btn => {
      btn.disabled = true;
      const o = parseInt(btn.dataset.o, 10);
      if (o === oi) btn.classList.add(correct ? 'quiz-opt-right' : 'quiz-opt-wrong');
      if (o === q.correct && !correct) btn.classList.add('quiz-opt-correct');
    });
    const verdictText = correct ? 'Right.' : 'Not quite.';
    fbEl.innerHTML = `<p class="quiz-fb"><strong class="${correct ? 'fb-good' : 'fb-bad'}">${verdictText}</strong> ${q.why}</p>`;

    if (answers.every(a => a !== null)) {
      const right = answers.filter((a, i) => a === QUESTIONS[i].correct).length;
      const onlyTaught = answers.filter((a, i) => a === QUESTIONS[i].correct && QUESTIONS[i].seenIn === 'taught').length;
      const summary = right === QUESTIONS.length
        ? `<strong>${right}/${QUESTIONS.length}.</strong> Every answer was on the taught surface. The bare diff alone could not have given you ${onlyTaught} of these.`
        : `<strong>${right}/${QUESTIONS.length}.</strong> The taught surface front-loads the answer to every question. The bare diff is silent on most of them — a reviewer reading the bare PR has to guess or ping the author.`;
      quizResult.innerHTML = `<div class="quiz-result-card">${summary}</div>`;
    }
  }

  renderQuiz();
</script>

<style is:global>
  .etude-page { max-width: 38rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0; }
  .etude-head { margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .etude-kicker {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: var(--label-size);
    letter-spacing: var(--label-tracking);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
  }
  .etude-title { font-family: var(--serif-display); font-size: 2.25rem; line-height: 1.15; margin: 0 0 0.5rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .etude-relief { font-family: var(--serif); font-style: italic; color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.05rem; margin: 0 0 1rem; line-height: 1.45; }
  .etude-nav { font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted); }
  .etude-nav a { color: var(--muted); text-decoration: none; }
  .etude-nav a:hover { color: var(--accent); }
  .etude-nav-sep { margin: 0 0.5rem; opacity: 0.5; }

  .etude-intro { margin: 0 0 1.5rem; }
  .etude-intro p { margin: 0 0 0.85rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .etude-stage { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.25rem; min-height: 22rem; }
  .etude-card {
    background: var(--bg-soft);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 1.5rem 1.5rem 1.25rem;
  }
  .etude-step {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: var(--label-size);
    letter-spacing: var(--label-tracking);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }

  /* === toggle === */
  .layer-toggle {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 0.55rem;
    margin: 0 0 1.2rem;
  }
  .layer-btn {
    appearance: none; -webkit-appearance: none;
    text-align: left;
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 0.65rem 0.85rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    color: var(--text);
    transition: border-color 180ms ease, background 180ms ease;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.15rem;
  }
  .layer-btn:hover:not(.layer-btn-active) { border-color: var(--muted); }
  .layer-btn-active {
    border-color: var(--accent);
    background: rgba(138, 52, 32, 0.05);
  }
  .layer-dot {
    display: inline-block;
    width: 0.55rem; height: 0.55rem; border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--line);
    margin-right: 0.5rem;
    vertical-align: middle;
  }
  .layer-btn-active .layer-dot { background: var(--accent); }
  .layer-name { font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.92rem; }
  .layer-meta {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  /* === bare PR === */
  .bare-pr {
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 0.85rem 1rem 0.6rem;
  }
  .bare-pr-head {
    display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.55rem; flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
  }
  .bare-pr-state {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    background: #2d7a3e; color: white;
    padding: 0.15rem 0.5rem;
    border-radius: 5px;
    text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; font-weight: 700;
  }
  .bare-pr-title {
    font-family: var(--serif-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .bare-pr-meta {
    margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .bare-pr-desc {
    margin: 0 0 0.85rem;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  /* === diff === */
  .d-file { margin: 0.55rem 0; }
  .d-file-name {
    font-family: ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    background: var(--bg-soft);
    padding: 0.32rem 0.55rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-bottom: none;
    border-radius: 6px 6px 0 0;
  }
  .d-hunk {
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 0 0 6px 6px;
    overflow-x: auto;
    font-family: ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .d-line { display: flex; padding: 0 0.55rem; white-space: pre; }
  .d-sigil { display: inline-block; width: 1.1rem; color: var(--muted); flex-shrink: 0; }
  .d-add { background: rgba(45, 122, 62, 0.08); color: #1a5a2e; }
  .d-add .d-sigil { color: #2d7a3e; }
  .d-del { background: rgba(138, 52, 32, 0.08); color: var(--accent); }
  .d-del .d-sigil { color: var(--accent); }
  .d-ctx { color: var(--text); }

  /* === teach === */
  .teach-wrap {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.1rem;
  }
  .teach-explain {
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-left: 3px solid #6fa8a4;
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 0.95rem 1.1rem;
  }
  .teach-card-title {
    font-family: var(--serif-display);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0 0 0.7rem;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .teach-row {
    margin: 0 0 0.65rem;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 5.5rem 1fr;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    align-items: start;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .teach-row-stack {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 0.35rem;
  }
  .teach-label {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-weight: 700;
    padding-top: 0.18rem;
  }
  .teach-body { color: var(--text); font-size: 0.92rem; }
  .teach-body code {
    font-family: ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    background: var(--bg-soft);
    padding: 0.05rem 0.32rem;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }
  .teach-list {
    margin: 0; padding: 0 0 0 1.1rem;
    color: var(--text); font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .teach-list li { margin: 0.2rem 0; }
  .teach-list code {
    font-family: ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    background: var(--bg-soft);
    padding: 0.05rem 0.32rem;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }
  .teach-diff-label {
    margin: 0 0 0.45rem;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /* === quiz === */
  .layer-quiz { margin: 0; }
  .quiz-help {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .quiz-list {
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: q;
    padding: 0; margin: 0;
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem;
  }
  .quiz-item {
    counter-increment: q;
    padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 8px;
  }
  .quiz-q::before {
    content: 'Q' counter(q) ' · ';
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .quiz-q {
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: 0.96rem;
  }
  .quiz-opts {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }
  .quiz-opt {
    appearance: none; -webkit-appearance: none;
    text-align: left;
    background: var(--bg-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 0.55rem 0.8rem;
    font-family: inherit;
    color: var(--text);
    cursor: pointer;
    line-height: 1.45;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    transition: border-color 180ms ease, background 180ms ease;
  }
  .quiz-opt:hover:not(:disabled) { border-color: var(--accent); }
  .quiz-opt:disabled { cursor: default; opacity: 0.7; }
  .quiz-opt-right { border-color: #2d7a3e; background: rgba(45, 122, 62, 0.08); opacity: 1; }
  .quiz-opt-wrong { border-color: var(--accent); background: rgba(138, 52, 32, 0.08); opacity: 1; }
  .quiz-opt-correct { border-color: #2d7a3e; background: rgba(45, 122, 62, 0.05); opacity: 1; }
  .quiz-feedback:not(:empty) { margin-top: 0.7rem; }
  .quiz-fb {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--text);
    line-height: 1.55;
    background: var(--bg-soft);
    padding: 0.5rem 0.7rem;
    border-radius: 5px;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--line);
  }
  .quiz-fb code {
    font-family: ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    background: var(--bg);
    padding: 0.05rem 0.3rem;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }
  .fb-good { color: #2d7a3e; margin-right: 0.4rem; }
  .fb-bad { color: var(--accent); margin-right: 0.4rem; }
